WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.105
The federal requirement, from NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three,

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.475
revision five, as the guide's
requirements table maps it.

3
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.684
Step 5 supports S C seven,
boundary protection, S C eight,

4
00:00:12.684 --> 00:00:17.079
transmission confidentiality
and integrity, and C P two,

5
00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:21.475
the contingency plan, which
the failover test exercises.

6
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:27.175
Its evidence is the origin lock-down test,
the TLS policy and the failover test.

7
00:00:27.175 --> 00:00:32.805
Step 6 supports S C seven and its enhancement
five, deny by default, and S I four,

8
00:00:32.805 --> 00:00:36.915
system monitoring; its evidence
is the firewall policy,

9
00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:39.775
the routes and the denied test request.

10
00:00:39.775 --> 00:00:42.510
Each row lines up with the fed-ramp twenty

11
00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:45.325
X key security indicators the guide names.

12
00:00:45.325 --> 00:00:50.267
The steps support these controls; the
organization still sets their parameters,

13
00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:53.500
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
